{"kind":"assert","text":"AE-1 independent source review of checkpoint 8353c4d7aaeb66e385f1a1afd37c2ea9f4461ea1 / tree278e68b0cc9d24187a4e158c04a93cb8e198d14b under final ruling50ce6650 and source act50be5471. This is not checker approval. No compiler, test, model, control, formatter, generator, build or gate ran; no reviewer source edit.\n\nDefinite fixture failure: packages/scope/test/archive-installed.test.ts:571 and585 construct application trust rows with only release/publisher. The real parser requires exact host,publisher,release keys (packages/client/src/application-trust.ts:23-25). ApplicationActAdmission.current at scope/src/applications/act-admission.ts:104-108 maps invalid trust to application-revoked. Therefore the positive allowed assertion at582 cannot pass, and the unrelated-release negative at586 tests malformed trust instead of release discrimination. Repair by taking the complete valid row from f.trust/bindings.APPLICATION_TRUST; vary only release for the unrelated case, preserving host/publisher. Sent this finding to the author/root without editing the subject. Apart from that trust setting, the actual root/child bytes, genuine Rules birth at the wrong parent address and real read APIs in551-579 form the intended joint comparison.\n\nTerminal prepayment correspondence: no current undercharge, new allowance or revival found in the reviewed slice. ArchiveDriver creates/selects its original budget at archive-driver.ts:153-155; after the existing terminal read it calls rows.prepareHalt(budget) exactly once at186, before own policy preparation at188-203 or later lookahead. prepareHalt at archive-row.ts:343-365 spends forecastArchiveTerminalWrite(512) once. The shared function at archive-row-cost.ts:93-96 prices calls2/metadata576/inputWork8192. The closure performs exactly two raw SQL INSERTs, terminal+tiny wake at360-361, inside one synchronous transaction, with original-budget check before/after at352/362 and no subsequent debit/refund/new budget. It